<Base title="Book processing credits" description="How Answer with Books credit purchases and hosted book charges work." path="/billing/credit-terms/">
 <article class="awb-section py-10 max-w-3xl">
  <p class="awb-eyebrow">Billing terms · October 9, 2026</p>
  <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl mt-3">Book processing credits</h1>
  <div class="mt-7 space-y-5 text-soft leading-relaxed">
   <p>Payments for Answer with Books are collected by Crowdlisten through Stripe. Credits represent a US-dollar account balance: a $5 top-up adds $5 to your balance. A top-up is a one-time purchase; it does not create a subscription or enable automatic reloads.</p>
   <p>Existing public books and your completed private book results are free to read, search, download, and reuse. Generating with your own agent has no Answer with Books generation charge; your agent provider may charge separately.</p>
   <p>A new hosted conversion shows an exact one-time price after source extraction. You must accept that price before generation begins. We reserve that amount from your available balance, then charge it once the book summary and skill are delivered. Status checks, downloads, and reuse do not create another conversion charge.</p>
   <p>If generation fails or you cancel unfinished work, the reservation is released to your available balance. Releasing a reservation is not a refund to your card: the unused funds stay in your account. Optional cover generation does not delay text delivery or settlement.</p>
   <p>Your uploaded sources and generated private results remain in your own library. Processing a different source or requesting a new revision can require another quote. Before accepting, review the source, options, amount, and expiration shown.</p>
   <p>Credits are added after payment is confirmed, not merely after returning from checkout. Your billing page lists the balance, conversion charges, and purchase receipts. If a payment is delayed or a charge seems incorrect, contact <a class="underline" href="mailto:terrychen2026@u.northwestern.edu?subject=Answer%20with%20Books%20billing">billing support</a>. You can also contact support to request a refund of unused credits.</p>
   <p>Generated summaries and skills can contain mistakes. Check important claims against the source citations. These payment terms supplement the <a class="underline" href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> and <a class="underline" href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <a class="awb-pill mt-8" href="/billing/">Back to billing</a>
 </article>
</Base>
